<article class="env-lemma" id="0F6Z">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0F6Z">Lemma <span data-tag="0F6Z">18.19.8</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{C}$ be a site. Let $U \in \mathop{\mathrm{Ob}}\nolimits (\mathcal{C})$. Assume that every $X$ in $\mathcal{C}$ has at most one morphism to $U$. Let $\mathcal{F}$ be an abelian sheaf on $\mathcal{C}/U$. The canonical maps $\mathcal{F} \to j_ U^{-1}j_{U!}\mathcal{F}$ and $j_ U^{-1}j_{U*}\mathcal{F} \to \mathcal{F}$ are isomorphisms. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is a special case of Lemma <a href="/tag/077I" data-tag="077I">18.16.4</a> because the assumption on $U$ is equivalent to the fully faithfulness of the localization functor $\mathcal{C}/U \to \mathcal{C}$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>